35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"I watched the entrance. Eleven bikes leave between seven and nine. Four times, someone had to shift another machine.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger shows little capital work. Any new system needs a levy. The treasurer spends three hours a month on cash.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The minutes show the same flats held covered spots for years. No review was ever recorded.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The complaint log has nine notes about leaning bikes. All died out because no one was responsible.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,The display frame trial took twenty seconds to load a bike. It needs greasing twice a year.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, if we charge, will people actually pay? The rain exposure is bad for uncovered spots.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ward park charges 2,600 yen. If we charge less, it might work. But the treasurer is already busy.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, twenty seconds is manageable. But who does the greasing?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, the sticker register shows some flats have three bikes. They said they would rather pay than be equal.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, that is useful. But the neighbouring block had arrears with a monthly charge.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The rain data confirms the covered spots are valuable. That explains the conflict.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A paid allocation could fund the maintenance. But we must ensure the treasurer isn't overwhelmed.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"If we use a lottery, it might feel fairer, but the minutes show people resist change.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Shared racks might reduce the ""shoving match,"" but the complaint log suggests we need clear responsibility.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,I think a paid system with clear rules is best. It covers the cost and defines responsibility.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Mio. The financial data supports a paid model.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I support the paid allocation. It is the only one with a clear revenue stream.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I am hesitant, but the data on arrears is concerning. Let us see the options.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I will vote for the option that minimizes social friction.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,Let us hope the vote is clear.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
